++// gauge_test.odin — v2-viscomm-gauge-telegraph's durable pins (the spec's
++// I/O & Edge-Case Matrix, one pin per row — the briefing's testing standard
++// is NON-NEGOTIABLE: every expectation here is a durable test, not PR prose):
++//
++//   (a) TABLE — EASE16 endpoints ([0]=0 continuity, [15]=1 exact arrival),
++//       strict monotone rise (an ease-out: fast start, settle), and the
++//       telegraph quality (motion visible within the first two entries).
++//   (b) HARNESS-INERT — the golden-stability contract: a zero-value (unfed)
++//       gauge reads raw EXACTLY for every tick — the capture path never
++//       feeds targets, so T2 goldens stay byte-identical by construction.
++//   (c) TWEEN — seed (first reading = raw, no 0->value fill at run start),
++//       no-pop at engage, monotone approach, exact arrival, stays-arrived.
++//   (d) CHASE — a mid-tween target move rides the same tween: the display
++//       change at the retarget tick is bounded by the raw's own move (no
++//       discontinuity larger than the underlying motion), then converges.
++//   (e) CHUNK — an instantaneous delta >= CHUNK_PCT fires the cue exactly
++//       once (alpha > 0 on the jump tick, 0 after len(CHUNK_FLASH) ticks),
++//       the tween re-anchors from the current display, and a LATER chunk
++//       re-fires (once per jump, not once ever). Sub-threshold never cues.
++//   (f) REDUCED MOTION — read snaps to raw, the feed never engages, the
++//       flash is suppressed; toggling motion back off-mid-run starts from
++//       truth (no stale tween, no fabricated chunk).
++//   (g) PAUSE/FREEZE — the phase derives from the tick: an unchanged tick
++//       renders the identical display (deterministic + tick-driven).
++//   (h) FEED (gauge_tick) — health/pool/sla targets land from live sim
++//       truth with the draws' own derivations (pool clamped 0..100; SLA
++//       avg/loss mirror draw_sla_gauges's raw math; roster > 8 unfed ->
++//       the zero-value raw fallback).
