+---
+title: 'viscomm(crisis): crisis-time desaturation of the non-involved network'
+type: 'feature'
+created: '2026-08-25'
+status: 'in-review'
+review_loop_iteration: 0
+context:
+  - briefing: /Users/moses/code/_bmad-output/briefs/packet-plumber-v2-viscomm-crisis-duck.md
+  - base: v2 (post #100 gauge-telegraph)
+---
+
+<frozen-after-approval reason="user design ruling 2026-08-25 (the parked question) — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** During an active crisis everything on the board screams equally — vibrant pipes, packets, and node accents keep their full saturation budget while the crisis telegraph (banner, rings, bottleneck outline) fights them for attention.
+
+**Approach (the user ruling):** desaturate the NON-INVOLVED network toward the board's calm register during an active crisis, so the crisis zone is the only saturated thing on the board. This reuses the v2-network-pop mechanism dynamically: vibrant network on calm paper, inverted under crisis — non-involved elements recede toward the paper.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- RENDER-SIDE ONLY. Read `state.crisis.active` (serialized rows); never alter crisis semantics, triggers, or resolve hysteresis. No core/ changes at all.
+- Involvement predicate (final, named in the PR): a BUNDLE is involved iff it is the named canonical `(bundle_lo, bundle_hi)` pair of an active `Saturated_Bundle` crisis. A NODE is involved iff it is an endpoint of an involved bundle. A PACKET is involved iff it rides an involved bundle (on-edge) or sits at an involved node (at-node). `Pool_Exhaustion` crises are map-wide — the whole network IS the crisis zone, so nothing recedes.
+- Desat math: plain arithmetic lerp toward `palette.canvas` by `CRISIS_DESAT_MIX (0.65) * factor` — no transcendentals (§10.4). Transition = pinned stepped table `CRISIS_FADE16` (PULSE16/EASE16 pattern), tick-driven, pure function of `(crisis rows, tick)` — no app feeding (the harness must render it; the pkt_interp/gauge zero-value precedent inverts here: the draw derives from sim rows directly).
+- **Byte-identical when inert:** zero active crises ⇒ factor exactly 0 ⇒ every render byte-identical (the wire-aesthetics standard). Proven by the zero-diff harness run.
+- Engage ramps over 16 ticks from the EARLIEST active onset; resolve LIFTS instantly (snap-back = the relief read + guarantees resolved frames return to canon bytes exactly; reduced-motion pins factor at 1.0 while any crisis is active — the static desat itself is NOT gated, only its transition).
+- Recede ONLY the network identity colors: pipe tier bands + casings + lane stripes, packet bodies/outlines, terminal family washes + type-chip glyphs, router tier washes/rings (primitive-path bodies too). NEVER the state triad / warning halos / health rings / crisis outline / banner (the telegraph family stays live), the drag ghost, selection/spawn/route-assist surfaces, or the LED (alive semantics, sub-pixel).
+- Golden discipline: T1/`.log.bin` byte-identical everywhere; crisis-carrying T2 frames re-blessed deliberately (predicted: juice@65s, surge@65s+149s, estate_surge@75s, a11y_×5@65s — the empirical run decides; snap-back keeps resolved captures byte-identical). Cause-document every re-blessed frame.
+- a11y: crisis separation (involved raw vs non-involved receded) must survive every CVD mode — pin as a palcheck pair with measured floors.
+- Fold PR #99 r2 advisories: W3 (route_tie inline-default coverage — stripped-JSON expect_color leg), W1+W2 (`_pr_body_viscomm_tie.md` mirror refresh to shipped r2 bytes).
+
+**Ask First:** (none — the ruling + briefing ranges cover it; the snap-back-on-resolve choice is documented in the PR's Decisions & rationale)
+
+**Never:**
+- No core/, catalog, or `data/balance.json` edits (cat.hash is golden-poison). `data/palette.json` untouched.
+- No new View state fed by the app (the factor derives purely from sim rows + tick).
+- No a11y mode-table edits (draw-time mixing over the effective palette is automatic).
+- No changes to goldens beyond the deliberate crisis-frame re-bless.
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Inert render | no active crises | factor 0; every draw byte-identical to pre-change | guard skips the mix entirely |
+| Engaged, non-involved bundle | crisis active, ramp done | tier band/casing/lanes mixed 65% toward canvas | — |
+| Engaged, involved bundle | named pair matches | raw saturated colors (untouched path) | — |
+| Pool_Exhaustion only | map-wide crisis | nothing recedes (whole network is the zone) | — |
+| Mid-ramp capture | onset < tick < onset+16 | factor = CRISIS_FADE16[phase] (deterministic) | — |
+| Resolve | last crisis resolves | factor snaps to 0 (byte-exact return) | — |
+| Reduced motion | any active crisis | factor pinned 1.0 (instant static desat) | — |
+| Overlapping crises | 2nd onset while active | phase still from EARLIEST onset (no reset) | — |
+| CVD mode active | any | recede uses the EFFECTIVE palette (remapped tiers + canvas) — separation survives, palcheck-pinned | — |
+| Hand-append guard | render fixture rows | fixture crises built via `pp.crisis_trigger` (the engine proc), never literal row appends (the 08-19 field-note trap) | — |
