+## Design Notes
+
+- Tween: `display = start + (target−start)·EASE16[phase]`, `phase = (tick − t0)·advance`; EASE16 = quadratic ease-out `{0, .129, .249, .36, .462, .556, .64, .716, .782, .84, .889, .929, .96, .982, .996, 1}` — [0]=0 pins no-pop continuity, [15]=1 pins exact arrival (== raw bytes).
+- Chunk ghost = fill-geometry rectangle between display and target levels, alpha = CHUNK_FLASH[tick−flash_t0] (fill, never lines — the rlsw line-alpha trap); fires once per threshold crossing (CHUNK_PCT = 25 units), life = len(CHUNK_FLASH).
+- Continuous small deltas ride the active tween (target chases raw, phase NOT reset — retarget continuity pinned); only a chunk re-anchors (start = current display).
+- SLA flash omitted (text row has no chunk geometry; the eased numbers kill the strobe) — decision recorded in PR Decisions & rationale.
+- Compile-time `when` guards: EASE16 endpoints, advance sanity, CHUNK_PCT range (the `BROKEN :: 1/0` idiom). Full no-transcendental enforcement is not compile-time-detectable in Odin — table-only math is the mechanism, review the guard.
